   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 760 gram  REMOVED_DATE x 15 x 2 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen  with an attached 24 x 10 4cm tan pink skin ellipse  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable nipple and no apparent scar  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm indurated gray white to tan yellow focally hemorrhagic mass which comes to 0 3cm of the inferior and 4 4cm of the deep margins  The remaining cut surface is 70  tan yellow adipose and 30  dense gray white fibrous tissue  The fibrous tissue is gritty to nodular with focal cystic change and is most extensive in the two inner quadrants  Sectioning of the axillary region reveals five tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  K L  Tumor to inferior margin M  Radial section of deep margin closest to tumor N O  Tumor P Q  Lower inner quadrant R  Upper inner quadrant S  Upper outer quadrant T  Lower outer quadrant U V  Lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect which is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 98  tan yellow adipose and 2  gray white fibrous cut surface with no lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as W GG  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M