 a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating medial  The specimen is inked black and overinked as anterior in blue  superior in green  inferior in yellow and lateral in red  Sectioning of the specimen from lateral to medial reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3cm tan white  irregularly shaped  firm area identified in the medial aspect of the specimen  which abuts the anterior  superior  inferior and deep margins  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes N U  Labeled  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm lymph node  The lymph node is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette V  Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3cm fibrofatty tissue which contains five lymph nodes ranging from 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  All of the lymph nodes are bivalved and submitted entirely in cassettes W AA  Resident  Mari Mino  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SMALL NODULE  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  ABUTTING THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  LARGE NODULE  SMALL FOCUS OF CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SCLEROSING  ADENOSIS  FIBROADENOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISIO PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MARGIN    EXCISION , NOS.
